    "shell.about.credits" : {
      "comment" : "The About panel's credits paragraph: what the app is, and the privacy posture that is the whole shape of the product — local first, more with the person's opt-in (2026-10-20). The self-check requires the words \"does not read\" and \"stays on this Mac\".",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Focus keeps track of your current priority and nudges you when the current content appears unrelated. It reads the active app. With your Accessibility opt-in, it also identifies the selected view or browser page. Browser answers can apply to one page, a path or a domain. Raw titles, URL credentials, queries and fragments are not stored. Focus does not read what you type or take screenshots. Local first: your data stays on this Mac unless you switch on Ask Decision-1, which lets Microsoft's Decision-1 see what Focus knows so it can judge your work better."
          }
        }
      }
    },
